commit b0f495735c30e400c9749c8b9f9823dbb56dfbd9
Author: Thiago Macieira <thiago.macieira@intel.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 19 17:21:15 2024 -0800

    QMetaType: remove legacy automatic name registrations for QObject-like

    This is wrong for cv-qualified T, because T::staticMetaObject is the
    same variable as the non-cv-qualified one, but isn't qualified. That
    causes a registration of `const MyObject *` to also register `MyObject
    *` with the same metatype.

    Even where it's right, it's unnecessary because we already have the
    names. This code was mostly added in 2012 for Qt 5.0; the only one that
    is still necessary of this lot is the case of pointer-to-gadget that
    registers the gadget itself.

    This removes the call to qRegisterNormalizedMetaTypeImplementation(),
    which has side-effects, but none of the types this matched are
    sequential containers, associative containers, pairs, smart pointers or
    QFuture.

    Fixes: QTBUG-147588
    Pick-to: 6.12 6.11 6.8
    Change-Id: I50b2a3e916ef23f21ebdfffdaf4d90317668802a
    Reviewed-by: Fabian Kosmale <fabian.kosmale@qt.io>

